/-!
# The finite group of signed monomials of a Clifford algebra

Let `b` be an orthogonal basis of a quadratic module `(M, Q)` whose generators square to `±1`, that
is `Q (b i) = 1` or `Q (b i) = -1` for every index `i`; over `ℂ` this is a normalized orthogonal
basis `e_i² = 1` of `ℂⁿ`. The subgroup `CliffordAlgebra.monomialGroup Q b` of the units of
`CliffordAlgebra Q` generated by `-1` and the generators `ι Q (b i)` is the group

`G = {±e_s : s a finite set of indices}`,

where `e_s = ι Q (b i₁) * ⋯ * ι Q (b iₖ)` for `s = {i₁ < ⋯ < iₖ}` is the basis vector
`CliffordAlgebra.basis Q b s`. Its multiplication is the sign rule
`CliffordAlgebra.basis_mul_basis`: `e_s * e_t = ±e_{s ∆ t}`. Its element `ε = -1` is central.
When the ring is nontrivial, `2` is invertible, and the finite index type has `n` elements,
the group is finite of order `2 ^ (n + 1)`.

That central element generates the **sign subgroup** `⟨ε⟩`, which is normal because it is central.
Every counting claim about it below assumes that `2 ≠ 0` in the Clifford algebra, which holds over
a nontrivial coefficient ring in which `2` is invertible; in characteristic two `ε = 1` and the sign
subgroup is trivial. Under that hypothesis `⟨ε⟩ = {1, ε}` has order two. Quotienting by it forgets
the sign of a signed monomial. The quotient is **commutative** for any family of pairwise
orthogonal vectors, because two such signed monomials commute or anticommute, so their commutator
is `1` or `ε`. When those pairwise orthogonal generators also square to `±1`, **every element of
the quotient has order dividing two** as well, because the square of such a signed monomial is `±1`;
for a finite orthogonal basis of `n` such generators over a ring as above the quotient has
`2 ^ n` elements, one for each index set `s`. The characters of `G` that kill `ε` are exactly the
characters of the quotient.

The group is a model of the Clifford algebra: the `e_s` form a basis of `CliffordAlgebra Q` and
multiply as the elements of `G` do, so the group algebra `R[G]` modulo the central element `ε + 1`
is the Clifford algebra. Sending each group element to its value gives an algebra map
`R[G] → CliffordAlgebra Q`. It is onto, since the generators lie in its image, and its kernel is
generated by `ε + 1`: every group element is `u` or `ε * u` for the element `u` of value `e_s`,
so modulo `ε + 1` every element of `R[G]` is a combination of these `u`, on which the map is
injective. Consequently an algebra map from the Clifford algebra to any `R`-algebra `A` is the same
as a monoid map `G → A` sending `ε` to `-1`; for `A = Module.End R W` this says that Clifford
modules are the representations of `G` in which `ε` acts by `-1`.

Any two signed monomials commute or anticommute, so conjugation can only change the sign of a
signed monomial, and a noncentral `u` is conjugate exactly to `u` and `-u`. The centre is `{±1}`
in even dimension `n` and `{±1, ±ω}` in odd dimension, for `ω = e_univ` the volume element, so the
class equation gives `2 ^ n + 1` conjugacy classes in even dimension and `2 ^ n + 2` in odd
dimension. By the character theory of finite groups, these also count the irreducible complex
representations of `G`.

Modulo `ε` only the support survives: `±e_s ↦ s` identifies `G / ⟨ε⟩` with the elementary abelian
group `(ZMod 2) ^ n`. Its characters are the sign characters `χ_t : ±e_s ↦ (-1) ^ #(s ∩ t)` for the
`2 ^ n` index sets `t`, and over a domain of characteristic not two these are all the characters
of `G` trivial on `ε`, each for exactly one `t`.

## Main definitions

* `CliffordAlgebra.monomialGroup Q v`: the subgroup of `(CliffordAlgebra Q)ˣ` generated by `-1`
  and the units whose value is a generator `ι Q (v i)`, for any family `v` of vectors.
* `CliffordAlgebra.monomialGroupEquiv`: the parametrization `(s, ε) ↦ ε • e_s` of the group by a
  finite index set and a sign.
* `CliffordAlgebra.monomialGroupEpsilon`: the central element `ε = -1`, the name under which the
  whole API below refers to it.
* `CliffordAlgebra.monomialGroupSign`: the central subgroup `⟨ε⟩` it generates.
* `CliffordAlgebra.monomialGroupSignCharEquiv`: the characters killing `ε` are the characters of
  the quotient by `⟨ε⟩`.
* `CliffordAlgebra.monomialGroupAlgHom Q v`: the algebra map from the group algebra of the group
  to the Clifford algebra, sending each group element to its value.
* `CliffordAlgebra.monomialGroupAlgebraQuotientEquiv`: **the Clifford algebra as the group algebra
  modulo `ε + 1`**.
* `CliffordAlgebra.monomialGroupLift`: algebra maps from the Clifford algebra are the monoid maps
  from the group sending `ε` to `-1`.
* `CliffordAlgebra.monomialGroupInvolute`: the grade involution, as an automorphism of the group.
* `CliffordAlgebra.monomialGroupSupport`: the support homomorphism `±e_s ↦ s` to `(ZMod 2) ^ I`.
* `CliffordAlgebra.monomialGroupQuotientEquiv`: **the quotient by `ε` is `(ZMod 2) ^ I`**.
* `CliffordAlgebra.monomialGroupCharacter`: the sign character `±e_s ↦ (-1) ^ #(s ∩ t)`.

## Main results

* `CliffordAlgebra.mem_monomialGroup_iff`: **the normal form**: a unit lies in the group exactly
  when its value is `e_s` or `-e_s` for some finite index set `s`.
* `CliffordAlgebra.mem_center_monomialGroup_iff`: a signed basis monomial is central exactly when
  its support is empty or is the full odd-cardinality index set.
* `CliffordAlgebra.monomialGroup_commuteOrNeg`: signed monomials commute or anticommute.
* `CliffordAlgebra.monomialGroup_val_eq_or_neg_of_isConj`: conjugation changes a signed monomial by
  at most its central sign.
* `CliffordAlgebra.monomialGroupEpsilon_mem_center`: `ε = -1` is central.
* `CliffordAlgebra.natCard_monomialGroup`: **the order** is `2 ^ (n + 1)` over a nontrivial
  ring in which `2` is invertible, and `CliffordAlgebra.finite_monomialGroup` is the finiteness
  that follows.
* `CliffordAlgebra.mem_monomialGroupSign_iff`: the sign subgroup is `{1, ε}`, and
  `CliffordAlgebra.natCard_monomialGroupSign`: it has order two whenever `2 ≠ 0` in the Clifford
  algebra, which `CliffordAlgebra.monomialGroupEpsilon_ne_one` turns into `ε ≠ 1`.
* `CliffordAlgebra.commutator_monomialGroup_le_monomialGroupSign` and
  `CliffordAlgebra.isMulCommutative_quotient_monomialGroupSign`: for a family of pairwise
  orthogonal vectors the quotient by the sign subgroup is commutative, and
  `CliffordAlgebra.exponent_quotient_monomialGroupSign_dvd_two`: when those vectors also square
  to `±1` its exponent divides two.
* `CliffordAlgebra.natCard_quotient_monomialGroupSign`: that quotient has `2 ^ n` elements, again
  over a nontrivial ring in which `2` is invertible.
* `CliffordAlgebra.monomialGroupAlgHom_surjective`: the group algebra maps onto the Clifford
  algebra whenever the vectors span and their squares are units.
* `CliffordAlgebra.ker_monomialGroupAlgHom`: for an orthogonal basis whose generators square to
  `±1`, the kernel of that map is the ideal generated by `ε + 1`.
* `CliffordAlgebra.monomialGroup_isConj_iff_of_notMem_center` and
  `CliffordAlgebra.natCard_carrier_monomialGroup_of_notMem_center`: a noncentral conjugacy class
  is `{u, -u}`, of size two.
* `CliffordAlgebra.monomialGroupEquiv_mem_center_iff`: the signed monomial `ε • e_s` is central
  exactly when its support `s` is empty or is the full odd-cardinality index set.
* `CliffordAlgebra.natCard_center_monomialGroup_of_even` and
  `CliffordAlgebra.natCard_center_monomialGroup_of_odd`: the centre has two elements in even
  dimension and four in odd dimension.
* `CliffordAlgebra.natCard_conjClasses_monomialGroup_of_even` and
  `CliffordAlgebra.natCard_conjClasses_monomialGroup_of_odd`: **the number of conjugacy classes**
  is `2 ^ n + 1` in even dimension `n` and `2 ^ n + 2` in odd dimension.
* `CliffordAlgebra.monomialGroup_hom_ext`: homomorphisms out of the group agree once they agree on
  `ε` and on the generators.
* `CliffordAlgebra.ker_monomialGroupSupport` and `CliffordAlgebra.monomialGroupSupport_surjective`:
  the support homomorphism is onto, with kernel `{1, ε}`.
* `CliffordAlgebra.existsUnique_monomialGroupCharacter_eq`: **the characters trivial on `ε` are
  the sign characters**, each for exactly one index set.

## References

* H. B. Lawson and M.-L. Michelsohn, *Spin Geometry* (1989), Chapter I, §1.
-/

public section

open scoped symmDiff

namespace CliffordAlgebra

variable {R M I : Type*} [CommRing R] [AddCommGroup M] [Module R M] (Q : QuadraticForm R M)

/-- The **group of signed monomials** of a family `v` of vectors: the subgroup of the units of
`CliffordAlgebra Q` generated by `-1` and the units whose value is a generator `ι Q (v i)`.

For a finite orthogonal basis whose generators square to `±1` it is the finite group of the `±e_s`
(`CliffordAlgebra.mem_monomialGroup_iff`). -/
def monomialGroup (v : I → M) : Subgroup (CliffordAlgebra Q)ˣ :=
  Subgroup.closure {u | (u : CliffordAlgebra Q) = -1 ∨ ∃ i, (u : CliffordAlgebra Q) = ι Q (v i)}

variable {Q} (v : I → M)

/-- The defining generators of the group of signed monomials. -/
theorem monomialGroup_def :
    monomialGroup Q v = Subgroup.closure {u : (CliffordAlgebra Q)ˣ |
      (u : CliffordAlgebra Q) = -1 ∨ ∃ i, (u : CliffordAlgebra Q) = ι Q (v i)} :=
  (rfl)

/-- The element `ε = -1` lies in the group of signed monomials. -/
theorem neg_one_mem_monomialGroup : -1 ∈ monomialGroup Q v :=
  Subgroup.subset_closure (Or.inl (by simp))

variable (Q) in
/-- **The central element `ε = -1`** of the group of signed monomials: the unit `-1`, viewed as an
element of the group. This is the canonical spelling of that element: every statement about it
below, up to the universal property `CliffordAlgebra.monomialGroupLift`, is phrased with this name
rather than with the anonymous constructor `⟨-1, neg_one_mem_monomialGroup v⟩`. -/
def monomialGroupEpsilon : monomialGroup Q v :=
  ⟨-1, neg_one_mem_monomialGroup v⟩

/-- The value of `ε` is the unit `-1`. -/
@[simp]
theorem coe_monomialGroupEpsilon :
    (monomialGroupEpsilon Q v : (CliffordAlgebra Q)ˣ) = -1 :=
  (rfl)

/-- `ε` squares to `1`. -/
@[simp]
theorem monomialGroupEpsilon_mul_self :
    monomialGroupEpsilon Q v * monomialGroupEpsilon Q v = 1 :=
  Subtype.ext (by simp)

/-- A unit whose value is a generator `ι Q (v i)` lies in the group of signed monomials. -/
theorem mem_monomialGroup_of_val_eq_ι {u : (CliffordAlgebra Q)ˣ} {i : I}
    (h : (u : CliffordAlgebra Q) = ι Q (v i)) : u ∈ monomialGroup Q v :=
  Subgroup.subset_closure (Or.inr ⟨i, h⟩)

/-- A generator `ι Q (v i)` with `Q (v i)` a unit is the value of an element of the group of signed
monomials. -/
theorem exists_monomialGroup_val_eq_ι {i : I} (h : IsUnit (Q (v i))) :
    ∃ g : monomialGroup Q v, ((g : (CliffordAlgebra Q)ˣ) : CliffordAlgebra Q) = ι Q (v i) := by
  obtain ⟨w, hw⟩ := isUnit_ι_of_isUnit Q h
  exact ⟨⟨w, mem_monomialGroup_of_val_eq_ι v hw⟩, hw⟩

/-- Two homomorphisms out of the group of signed monomials are equal once they agree on `ε = -1`
and on the units whose value is a generator `ι Q (v i)`. -/
theorem monomialGroup_hom_ext {N : Type*} [Monoid N] {f f' : monomialGroup Q v →* N}
    (hε : f (monomialGroupEpsilon Q v) = f' (monomialGroupEpsilon Q v))
    (hι : ∀ (g : monomialGroup Q v) (i : I),
      ((g : (CliffordAlgebra Q)ˣ) : CliffordAlgebra Q) = ι Q (v i) → f g = f' g) :
    f = f' := by
  have htop : Subgroup.closure ((monomialGroup Q v).subtype ⁻¹' {u : (CliffordAlgebra Q)ˣ |
      (u : CliffordAlgebra Q) = -1 ∨ ∃ i, (u : CliffordAlgebra Q) = ι Q (v i)}) = ⊤ :=
    Subgroup.closure_preimage_eq_top _
  refine MonoidHom.eq_of_eqOn_dense htop ?_
  rintro x (hx | ⟨i, hx⟩)
  · obtain rfl : x = monomialGroupEpsilon Q v := Subtype.ext (Units.ext hx)
    exact hε
  · exact hι x i hx

/-- **The element `ε = -1` is central** in the group of signed monomials. -/
theorem monomialGroupEpsilon_mem_center :
    monomialGroupEpsilon Q v ∈ Subgroup.center (monomialGroup Q v) :=
  Subgroup.mem_center_iff.mpr fun _ ↦ Subtype.ext (Units.ext (by simp))

/-- The grade involution maps the group of signed monomials into itself: it fixes `-1` and sends
a generator `ι Q (v i)` to `-ι Q (v i)`. -/
theorem units_map_involute_mem_monomialGroup {u : (CliffordAlgebra Q)ˣ}
    (hu : u ∈ monomialGroup Q v) :
    Units.map (involute : CliffordAlgebra Q →ₐ[R] _).toMonoidHom u ∈ monomialGroup Q v := by
  rw [monomialGroup_def] at hu ⊢
  induction hu using Subgroup.closure_induction with
  | mem u hu =>
    rcases hu with hu | ⟨i, hu⟩
    · exact Subgroup.subset_closure (Or.inl (by simp [hu]))
    · -- The image `-ι Q (v i)` is the product of `-1` and the generator `ι Q (v i)`.
      have h : Units.map (involute : CliffordAlgebra Q →ₐ[R] _).toMonoidHom u = -1 * u :=
        Units.ext (by simp [hu])
      rw [h]
      exact mul_mem (Subgroup.subset_closure (Or.inl rfl))
        (Subgroup.subset_closure (Or.inr ⟨i, hu⟩))
  | one => simp
  | mul u w _ _ hu hw => simpa using mul_mem hu hw
  | inv u _ hu => simpa using inv_mem hu

/-- **The grade involution as an automorphism of the group of signed monomials.** For an orthogonal
basis it sends the signed monomial `±e_s` to `±(-1) ^ #s e_s`. -/
noncomputable def monomialGroupInvolute : monomialGroup Q v ≃* monomialGroup Q v where
  toFun g := ⟨_, units_map_involute_mem_monomialGroup v g.2⟩
  invFun g := ⟨_, units_map_involute_mem_monomialGroup v g.2⟩
  left_inv _ := Subtype.ext (Units.ext (involute_involute _))
  right_inv _ := Subtype.ext (Units.ext (involute_involute _))
  map_mul' _ _ := Subtype.ext (map_mul _ _ _)

/-- The value of the image of a signed monomial under `CliffordAlgebra.monomialGroupInvolute` is
the grade involution of its value. -/
@[simp]
theorem coe_monomialGroupInvolute_apply (g : monomialGroup Q v) :
    ((monomialGroupInvolute v g : (CliffordAlgebra Q)ˣ) : CliffordAlgebra Q) =
      involute ((g : (CliffordAlgebra Q)ˣ) : CliffordAlgebra Q) :=
  (rfl)

/-- `CliffordAlgebra.monomialGroupInvolute` is its own inverse. -/
@[simp]
theorem monomialGroupInvolute_symm :
    (monomialGroupInvolute v).symm = monomialGroupInvolute (Q := Q) v :=
  (rfl)

/-! ### The sign subgroup generated by `ε` -/

variable (Q) in
/-- **The sign subgroup `⟨ε⟩`** of the group of signed monomials: the central subgroup generated by
`ε = -1`. Quotienting by it forgets the sign of a signed monomial. -/
def monomialGroupSign : Subgroup (monomialGroup Q v) :=
  Subgroup.zpowers (monomialGroupEpsilon Q v)

/-- The sign subgroup is the subgroup generated by `ε`, which gives access to Mathlib's
`Subgroup.zpowers` API. -/
theorem monomialGroupSign_def :
    monomialGroupSign Q v = Subgroup.zpowers (monomialGroupEpsilon Q v) :=
  (rfl)

/-- `ε` lies in the sign subgroup it generates. This is not a `simp` lemma: the `simp` form of its
statement is `CliffordAlgebra.mem_monomialGroupSign_iff`, which already proves it. -/
theorem monomialGroupEpsilon_mem_monomialGroupSign :
    monomialGroupEpsilon Q v ∈ monomialGroupSign Q v :=
  Subgroup.mem_zpowers _

/-- **The sign subgroup is `{1, ε}`**: `ε` squares to `1`, so its powers are itself and the
identity. -/
@[simp]
theorem mem_monomialGroupSign_iff {u : monomialGroup Q v} :
    u ∈ monomialGroupSign Q v ↔ u = 1 ∨ u = monomialGroupEpsilon Q v := by
  refine ⟨?_, ?_⟩
  · rw [monomialGroupSign_def, Subgroup.mem_zpowers_iff]
    rintro ⟨k, rfl⟩
    rcases Int.even_or_odd k with ⟨m, rfl⟩ | ⟨m, rfl⟩
    · exact Or.inl (by
        rw [← two_mul, zpow_mul, zpow_two, monomialGroupEpsilon_mul_self, one_zpow])
    · exact Or.inr (by
        rw [zpow_add_one, zpow_mul, zpow_two, monomialGroupEpsilon_mul_self, one_zpow, one_mul])
  · rintro (rfl | rfl)
    · exact one_mem _
    · exact monomialGroupEpsilon_mem_monomialGroupSign v

instance monomialGroupSign_normal : (monomialGroupSign Q v).Normal :=
  Subgroup.normal_of_le_center (Subgroup.zpowers_le.mpr (monomialGroupEpsilon_mem_center v))

/-- **`ε` is not the identity** as soon as `2 ≠ 0` in the Clifford algebra: the value of `ε` is the
unit `-1`, and `-1 = 1` says exactly that `2 = 0`. Over a nontrivial coefficient ring in which `2`
is invertible the hypothesis is discharged by `two_ne_zero`, since the scalars of the Clifford
algebra are a faithful copy of `R` (`CliffordAlgebra.neZeroTwo`). -/
theorem monomialGroupEpsilon_ne_one (h2 : (2 : CliffordAlgebra Q) ≠ 0) :
    monomialGroupEpsilon Q v ≠ 1 := by
  intro h
  have h1 : (-1 : CliffordAlgebra Q) = 1 := by
    simpa using congrArg (fun g : monomialGroup Q v ↦
      ((g : (CliffordAlgebra Q)ˣ) : CliffordAlgebra Q)) h
  exact h2 (by rw [← one_add_one_eq_two, ← sub_neg_eq_add, h1, sub_self])

/-- **The sign subgroup has order two** whenever `2 ≠ 0` in the Clifford algebra: `ε` squares to
`1` and, by `CliffordAlgebra.monomialGroupEpsilon_ne_one`, is not `1`. -/
theorem natCard_monomialGroupSign (h2 : (2 : CliffordAlgebra Q) ≠ 0) :
    Nat.card (monomialGroupSign Q v) = 2 := by
  rw [monomialGroupSign_def, Nat.card_zpowers]
  exact orderOf_eq_prime (by rw [pow_two, monomialGroupEpsilon_mul_self])
    (monomialGroupEpsilon_ne_one v h2)

/-! ### Commutation and conjugation of signed monomials -/

/-- Any two signed monomials commute or anticommute, without a normalization assumption on their
generator squares. -/
lemma monomialGroup_commuteOrNeg
    (v : I → M) (hv : ∀ i j, i ≠ j → Q.IsOrtho (v i) (v j))
    (c u : monomialGroup Q v) :
    TauCeti.CommuteOrNeg (c : (CliffordAlgebra Q)ˣ) u := by
  let S : Set (CliffordAlgebra Q)ˣ := {x | (x : CliffordAlgebra Q) = -1 ∨
    ∃ i, (x : CliffordAlgebra Q) = ι Q (v i)}
  have hgen : ∀ x ∈ S, ∀ y ∈ S, TauCeti.CommuteOrNeg x y := by
    intro x hx y hy
    dsimp [S] at hx hy
    rcases hx with hx | ⟨i, hx⟩ <;> rcases hy with hy | ⟨j, hy⟩
    · apply TauCeti.CommuteOrNeg.of_commute
      apply Units.ext
      simp [hx, hy]
    · apply TauCeti.CommuteOrNeg.of_commute
      apply Units.ext
      simp [hx, hy]
    · apply TauCeti.CommuteOrNeg.of_commute
      apply Units.ext
      simp [hx, hy]
    · by_cases hij : i = j
      · subst j
        apply TauCeti.CommuteOrNeg.of_commute
        apply Units.ext
        simp [hx, hy]
      · apply TauCeti.CommuteOrNeg.of_semiconjBy
        apply Units.ext
        simpa [hx, hy] using ι_mul_ι_comm_of_isOrtho (hv i j hij)
  have hmonomial : monomialGroup Q v = Subgroup.closure S := by
    simpa only [S] using (monomialGroup_def (Q := Q) v)
  have hc : (c : (CliffordAlgebra Q)ˣ) ∈ Subgroup.closure S := by
    rw [← hmonomial]
    exact c.property
  have hu : (u : (CliffordAlgebra Q)ˣ) ∈ Subgroup.closure S := by
    rw [← hmonomial]
    exact u.property
  exact TauCeti.CommuteOrNeg.of_mem_closure hgen hc hu

/-- Every conjugate of a signed Clifford monomial is itself or its negative. -/
lemma monomialGroup_val_eq_or_neg_of_isConj
    (v : I → M) (hv : ∀ i j, i ≠ j → Q.IsOrtho (v i) (v j))
    {u w : monomialGroup Q v} (h : IsConj u w) :
  (w : (CliffordAlgebra Q)ˣ) = (u : (CliffordAlgebra Q)ˣ) ∨
      (w : (CliffordAlgebra Q)ˣ) = -(u : (CliffordAlgebra Q)ˣ) := by
  obtain ⟨c, hc⟩ := isConj_iff.mp h
  have hmul := congrArg (fun z : monomialGroup Q v => (z : (CliffordAlgebra Q)ˣ) * c) hc
  have hcv : (c : (CliffordAlgebra Q)ˣ) * u = (w : (CliffordAlgebra Q)ˣ) * c := by
    simpa [mul_assoc] using hmul
  have hcu := monomialGroup_commuteOrNeg v hv c u
  rcases TauCeti.CommuteOrNeg.out hcu with hcu | hcu
  · left
    have hcancel : (w : (CliffordAlgebra Q)ˣ) * c = (u : (CliffordAlgebra Q)ˣ) * c :=
      hcv.symm.trans hcu.eq
    exact mul_right_cancel_iff.mp hcancel
  · right
    have hcancel : (w : (CliffordAlgebra Q)ˣ) * c = (-(u : (CliffordAlgebra Q)ˣ)) * c := by
      calc
        (w : (CliffordAlgebra Q)ˣ) * c = (c : (CliffordAlgebra Q)ˣ) * u := hcv.symm
        _ = (-(u : (CliffordAlgebra Q)ˣ)) * c := hcu.eq
    exact mul_right_cancel_iff.mp hcancel

/-! ### The quotient by the sign subgroup -/

/-- **The commutator of two signed monomials lies in the sign subgroup.** Signed monomials of
pairwise orthogonal generators commute or anticommute, so their commutator is `1` or `ε`;
`CliffordAlgebra.commutator_monomialGroup_le_monomialGroupSign` is the subgroup form. -/
theorem inv_mul_mul_comm_mem_monomialGroupSign
    (hv : ∀ i j, i ≠ j → Q.IsOrtho (v i) (v j)) (c u : monomialGroup Q v) :
    (c * u)⁻¹ * (u * c) ∈ monomialGroupSign Q v := by
  rcases (monomialGroup_commuteOrNeg v hv c u).out with h | h
  · refine (mem_monomialGroupSign_iff v).mpr (Or.inl ?_)
    rw [inv_mul_eq_one]
    exact Subtype.ext h.eq
  · refine (mem_monomialGroupSign_iff v).mpr (Or.inr (Subtype.ext ?_))
    have hcu : ((c * u : monomialGroup Q v) : (CliffordAlgebra Q)ˣ)
        = -((u * c : monomialGroup Q v) : (CliffordAlgebra Q)ˣ) := by
      simpa [neg_mul] using h.eq
    push_cast [hcu]
    simp

/-- **The commutator subgroup of the group of signed monomials lies in the sign subgroup**, which
is the subgroup form of `CliffordAlgebra.inv_mul_mul_comm_mem_monomialGroupSign`. -/
theorem commutator_monomialGroup_le_monomialGroupSign
    (hv : ∀ i j, i ≠ j → Q.IsOrtho (v i) (v j)) :
    commutator (monomialGroup Q v) ≤ monomialGroupSign Q v := by
  rw [commutator_def, Subgroup.commutator_le]
  intro c _ u _
  have hcomm : c * u * c⁻¹ * u⁻¹ = (u⁻¹ * c⁻¹)⁻¹ * (c⁻¹ * u⁻¹) := by group
  rw [commutatorElement_def, hcomm]
  exact inv_mul_mul_comm_mem_monomialGroupSign v hv u⁻¹ c⁻¹

/-- **The quotient of the group of signed monomials by its sign subgroup is commutative**, because
the commutator subgroup lies in the sign subgroup. -/
theorem isMulCommutative_quotient_monomialGroupSign
    (hv : ∀ i j, i ≠ j → Q.IsOrtho (v i) (v j)) :
    IsMulCommutative (monomialGroup Q v ⧸ monomialGroupSign Q v) :=
  Subgroup.Normal.quotient_commutative_iff_commutator_le.mpr
    (commutator_monomialGroup_le_monomialGroupSign v hv)

/-- **A signed monomial squares into the sign subgroup**: when pairwise orthogonal generators
square to `±1`, the square of every signed monomial is `±1`. The generators square to `±1`, and
since two signed monomials commute or anticommute, `(x * y) * (x * y) = ±(x * x) * (y * y)`. -/
theorem mul_self_mem_monomialGroupSign (hv : ∀ i j, i ≠ j → Q.IsOrtho (v i) (v j))
    (hQ : ∀ i, Q (v i) = 1 ∨ Q (v i) = -1) (u : monomialGroup Q v) :
    u * u ∈ monomialGroupSign Q v := by
  have key {x : (CliffordAlgebra Q)ˣ} (hx : x ∈ monomialGroup Q v) : x * x = 1 ∨ x * x = -1 := by
    rw [monomialGroup_def] at hx
    induction hx using Subgroup.closure_induction with
    | mem x hx =>
      rcases hx with hx | ⟨i, hx⟩
      · exact Or.inl (Units.ext (by simp [hx]))
      · rcases hQ i with h | h
        · exact Or.inl (Units.ext (by simp [hx, ι_sq_scalar, h]))
        · exact Or.inr (Units.ext (by simp [hx, ι_sq_scalar, h]))
    | one => simp
    | mul x y hx hy ihx ihy =>
      have e : x * y * (x * y) = x * x * (y * y) ∨ x * y * (x * y) = -(x * x * (y * y)) := by
        rcases (monomialGroup_commuteOrNeg v hv ⟨x, hx⟩ ⟨y, hy⟩).out with h | h
        · have h' : y * x = x * y := h.eq.symm
          left
          rw [mul_assoc, ← mul_assoc y, h']
          simp only [mul_assoc]
        · have h' : y * x = -(x * y) := by
            have h'' : x * y = -y * x := h.eq
            rw [h'', neg_mul, neg_neg]
          right
          rw [mul_assoc, ← mul_assoc y, h']
          simp only [neg_mul, mul_neg, mul_assoc]
      rcases e with e | e <;> rcases ihx with h1 | h1 <;> rcases ihy with h2 | h2 <;>
        simp [e, h1, h2]
    | inv x hx ih =>
      rw [← mul_inv_rev]
      rcases ih with h | h <;> simp [h]
  refine (mem_monomialGroupSign_iff v).mpr ?_
  rcases key u.2 with h | h
  · exact Or.inl (Subtype.ext h)
  · exact Or.inr (Subtype.ext h)

/-- **The quotient by the sign subgroup has exponent dividing two** when pairwise orthogonal
generators square to `±1`. -/
theorem exponent_quotient_monomialGroupSign_dvd_two
    (hv : ∀ i j, i ≠ j → Q.IsOrtho (v i) (v j)) (hQ : ∀ i, Q (v i) = 1 ∨ Q (v i) = -1) :
    Monoid.exponent (monomialGroup Q v ⧸ monomialGroupSign Q v) ∣ 2 := by
  refine Monoid.exponent_dvd_of_forall_pow_eq_one fun x ↦ ?_
  induction x using QuotientGroup.induction_on with | H u =>
  rw [pow_two, ← QuotientGroup.mk_mul, QuotientGroup.eq_one_iff]
  exact mul_self_mem_monomialGroupSign v hv hQ u

/-- **The characters of the group of signed monomials that send `ε` to `1` are the characters of
the quotient by the sign subgroup.** A character kills `ε` exactly when it kills the subgroup `ε`
generates, so it factors through the quotient. The values are allowed in any group, so this covers
the characters with values in the units of a ring as well as the sign characters. -/
def monomialGroupSignCharEquiv {H : Type*} [Group H] :
    {χ : monomialGroup Q v →* H // χ (monomialGroupEpsilon Q v) = 1} ≃
      ((monomialGroup Q v ⧸ monomialGroupSign Q v) →* H) where
  toFun χ := QuotientGroup.lift _ χ.1 fun u hu ↦ by
    rcases (mem_monomialGroupSign_iff v).mp hu with rfl | rfl
    · exact map_one _
    · exact χ.2
  invFun ψ := ⟨ψ.comp (QuotientGroup.mk' (monomialGroupSign Q v)), by
    have hε := (QuotientGroup.eq_one_iff (N := monomialGroupSign Q v)
      (monomialGroupEpsilon Q v)).mpr (monomialGroupEpsilon_mem_monomialGroupSign v)
    simp [hε]⟩
  left_inv _ := Subtype.ext (MonoidHom.ext fun _ ↦ rfl)
  right_inv ψ := MonoidHom.ext fun x ↦ by
    induction x using QuotientGroup.induction_on with | H u => rfl

/-- `CliffordAlgebra.monomialGroupSignCharEquiv` sends a monoid map killing `ε` to the map of the
quotient taking the class of a group element to its value. -/
@[simp]
theorem monomialGroupSignCharEquiv_apply_mk {H : Type*} [Group H]
    (χ : {χ : monomialGroup Q v →* H // χ (monomialGroupEpsilon Q v) = 1})
    (u : monomialGroup Q v) :
    monomialGroupSignCharEquiv v χ (QuotientGroup.mk u) = χ.1 u :=
  (rfl)

/-- The inverse of `CliffordAlgebra.monomialGroupSignCharEquiv` sends a monoid map of the quotient
to its composite with the quotient map. -/
@[simp]
theorem monomialGroupSignCharEquiv_symm_apply_coe {H : Type*} [Group H]
    (ψ : (monomialGroup Q v ⧸ monomialGroupSign Q v) →* H) (u : monomialGroup Q v) :
    ((monomialGroupSignCharEquiv v).symm ψ).1 u = ψ (QuotientGroup.mk u) :=
  (rfl)

/-! ### The group algebra of the group of signed monomials -/

variable (Q) in
/-- The algebra map from the group algebra of the group of signed monomials to the Clifford
algebra, sending each group element to its value. -/
noncomputable def monomialGroupAlgHom :
    MonoidAlgebra R (monomialGroup Q v) →ₐ[R] CliffordAlgebra Q :=
  MonoidAlgebra.lift R (CliffordAlgebra Q) (monomialGroup Q v)
    ((Units.coeHom (CliffordAlgebra Q)).comp (monomialGroup Q v).subtype)

/-- `CliffordAlgebra.monomialGroupAlgHom` sends a group element to its value. -/
theorem monomialGroupAlgHom_of (g : monomialGroup Q v) :
    monomialGroupAlgHom Q v (MonoidAlgebra.of R (monomialGroup Q v) g) =
      ((g : (CliffordAlgebra Q)ˣ) : CliffordAlgebra Q) :=
  MonoidAlgebra.lift_of ..

/-- `CliffordAlgebra.monomialGroupAlgHom` sends `r` times a group element to `r` times its
value. -/
@[simp]
theorem monomialGroupAlgHom_single (g : monomialGroup Q v) (r : R) :
    monomialGroupAlgHom Q v (MonoidAlgebra.single g r) =
      r • ((g : (CliffordAlgebra Q)ˣ) : CliffordAlgebra Q) :=
  MonoidAlgebra.lift_single ..

/-- The element `ε + 1` of the group algebra, for `ε = -1` the central element of the group of
signed monomials, lies in the kernel of `CliffordAlgebra.monomialGroupAlgHom`. -/
theorem monomialGroupAlgHom_of_monomialGroupEpsilon_add_one_eq_zero :
    monomialGroupAlgHom Q v
      (MonoidAlgebra.of R (monomialGroup Q v) (monomialGroupEpsilon Q v) + 1) = 0 := by
  simp

/-- The element `ε + 1` of the group algebra is central. -/
private theorem of_monomialGroupEpsilon_add_one_mem_center :
    MonoidAlgebra.of R (monomialGroup Q v) (monomialGroupEpsilon Q v) + 1 ∈
      Set.center (MonoidAlgebra R (monomialGroup Q v)) :=
  Semigroup.mem_center_iff.mpr fun y ↦
    ((MonoidAlgebra.of_commute (fun g ↦
      ((Subgroup.mem_center_iff.mp (monomialGroupEpsilon_mem_center v) g).symm)) y).add_left
        (Commute.one_left y)).eq.symm

/-- Multiplying a group element `g` by `ε + 1` gives `ε * g + g`. -/
private theorem of_monomialGroupEpsilon_mul_add_of (g : monomialGroup Q v) :
    MonoidAlgebra.of R _ (monomialGroupEpsilon Q v * g) + MonoidAlgebra.of R _ g =
      MonoidAlgebra.of R _ g *
        (MonoidAlgebra.of R (monomialGroup Q v) (monomialGroupEpsilon Q v) + 1) := by
  rw [mul_add, mul_one, ← map_mul,
    Subgroup.mem_center_iff.mp (monomialGroupEpsilon_mem_center v) g]

/-- The left ideal generated by the central element `ε + 1` of the group algebra is two-sided. -/
instance isTwoSided_span_of_monomialGroupEpsilon_add_one :
    (Ideal.span {MonoidAlgebra.of R (monomialGroup Q v) (monomialGroupEpsilon Q v) +
      1}).IsTwoSided :=
  Ideal.isTwoSided_span_of_subset_center
    (Set.singleton_subset_iff.mpr (of_monomialGroupEpsilon_add_one_mem_center v))

/-- **The group algebra maps onto the Clifford algebra** when the vectors `v` span `M` and the
generators `ι Q (v i)` are units, that is, when every `Q (v i)` is a unit. -/
theorem monomialGroupAlgHom_surjective (hv : Submodule.span R (Set.range v) = ⊤)
    (hQ : ∀ i, IsUnit (Q (v i))) : Function.Surjective (monomialGroupAlgHom Q v) := by
  rw [← AlgHom.range_eq_top, eq_top_iff, ← adjoin_range_ι, Algebra.adjoin_le_iff]
  -- The vectors whose generator lies in the range form a submodule containing every `v i`.
  have hle : Submodule.span R (Set.range v) ≤
      (Subalgebra.toSubmodule (monomialGroupAlgHom Q v).range).comap (ι Q) := by
    refine Submodule.span_le.mpr ?_
    rintro _ ⟨i, rfl⟩
    obtain ⟨g, hg⟩ := exists_monomialGroup_val_eq_ι v (hQ i)
    exact ⟨MonoidAlgebra.of R _ g, by simp [hg]⟩
  rintro _ ⟨m, rfl⟩
  exact hle (hv ▸ Submodule.mem_top)

/-- A generator squaring to `±1` squares to a unit. -/
private theorem isUnit_of_eq_one_or_neg_one (hQ : ∀ i, Q (v i) = 1 ∨ Q (v i) = -1) (i : I) :
    IsUnit (Q (v i)) := by
  rcases hQ i with h | h <;> simp [h]

variable [Invertible (2 : R)] [LinearOrder I] {b : Module.Basis I R M}

/-- **The normal form of the group of signed monomials**: for an orthogonal basis whose generators
square to `±1`, a unit lies in `CliffordAlgebra.monomialGroup Q b` exactly when its value is
`e_s` or `-e_s` for a finite index set `s`. -/
theorem mem_monomialGroup_iff (hb : (QuadraticMap.associated Q).IsOrthoᵢ b)
    (hQ : ∀ i, Q (b i) = 1 ∨ Q (b i) = -1) {u : (CliffordAlgebra Q)ˣ} :
    u ∈ monomialGroup Q b ↔
      ∃ s, (u : CliffordAlgebra Q) = basis Q b s ∨ (u : CliffordAlgebra Q) = -basis Q b s := by
  constructor
  · -- The signed monomials contain the generators and are closed under products and inverses.
    intro hu
    induction hu using Subgroup.closure_induction with
    | mem u hu =>
      rcases hu with hu | ⟨i, hu⟩
      · exact ⟨∅, Or.inr (by rw [hu, basis_empty])⟩
      · exact ⟨{i}, Or.inl (by rw [hu, basis_singleton])⟩
    | one => exact ⟨∅, Or.inl (by rw [Units.val_one, basis_empty])⟩
    | mul u v _ _ hu hv =>
      obtain ⟨s, hs⟩ := hu
      obtain ⟨t, ht⟩ := hv
      refine ⟨s ∆ t, ?_⟩
      rw [Units.val_mul]
      rcases basis_mul_basis_eq_or hb hQ s t with h | h <;>
        rcases hs with hs | hs <;> rcases ht with ht | ht <;>
        simp only [hs, ht, neg_mul, mul_neg, neg_neg, h, true_or, or_true]
    | inv u _ hu =>
      obtain ⟨s, hs⟩ := hu
      refine ⟨s, ?_⟩
      -- `u * u = ±1`, so `u⁻¹ = ±u`.
      have huu : (u : CliffordAlgebra Q) * u = 1 ∨ (u : CliffordAlgebra Q) * u = -1 := by
        rcases hs with hs | hs <;> simpa only [hs, neg_mul_neg] using basis_mul_self_eq_or hb hQ s
      rcases huu with h | h
      · rw [Units.inv_eq_of_mul_eq_one_right h]
        exact hs
      · have hneg : (u : CliffordAlgebra Q) * -u = 1 := by rw [mul_neg, h, neg_neg]
        rw [Units.inv_eq_of_mul_eq_one_right hneg]
        rcases hs with hs | hs <;> rw [hs] <;> simp
  · -- Peel off the generators one at a time, starting from the least index.
    rintro ⟨s, hs⟩
    induction s using Finset.induction_on_min generalizing u with
    | empty =>
      rw [basis_empty] at hs
      rcases hs with hs | hs
      · rw [Units.val_eq_one.mp hs]
        exact one_mem _
      · exact Subgroup.subset_closure (Or.inl hs)
    | insert a s ha ih =>
      -- The generator of `a` squares to `Q (b a) = ±1`, so it is a unit.
      have hsq : Q (b a) * Q (b a) = 1 := by rcases hQ a with h | h <;> rw [h] <;> norm_num
      let : Invertible (Q (b a)) := ⟨Q (b a), hsq, hsq⟩
      let := invertibleιOfInvertible Q (b a)
      let g := unitOfInvertible (ι Q (b a))
      have hg : g ∈ monomialGroup Q b := mem_monomialGroup_of_val_eq_ι b rfl
      have hgu : g⁻¹ * u ∈ monomialGroup Q b := by
        refine ih ?_
        rw [basis_insert_of_forall_lt hb ha] at hs
        -- Mathlib's `unitOfInvertible` has value `ι Q (b a)` and inverse `⅟(ι Q (b a))`.
        simp only [g, unitOfInvertible, Units.inv_mk, Units.val_mul]
        rcases hs with hs | hs
        · exact Or.inl (by rw [hs, invOf_mul_cancel_left])
        · exact Or.inr (by rw [hs, mul_neg, invOf_mul_cancel_left])
      simpa using mul_mem hg hgu

/-- For an orthogonal basis whose generators square to `±1`, every basis vector `e_s` is the value
of an element of the group of signed monomials. -/
theorem exists_monomialGroup_val_eq_basis (hb : (QuadraticMap.associated Q).IsOrthoᵢ b)
    (hQ : ∀ i, Q (b i) = 1 ∨ Q (b i) = -1) (s : Finset I) :
    ∃ u : monomialGroup Q b, ((u : (CliffordAlgebra Q)ˣ) : CliffordAlgebra Q) = basis Q b s := by
  obtain ⟨u, hu⟩ := isUnit_basis hb s fun i _ ↦ isUnit_of_eq_one_or_neg_one b hQ i
  exact ⟨⟨u, (mem_monomialGroup_iff hb hQ).mpr ⟨s, Or.inl hu⟩⟩, hu⟩

/-- For an orthogonal basis whose generators square to `±1`, every signed basis vector `ε • e_s`
is the value of an element of the group of signed monomials. -/
private theorem exists_monomialGroup_val_eq_zsmul_basis
    (hb : (QuadraticMap.associated Q).IsOrthoᵢ b) (hQ : ∀ i, Q (b i) = 1 ∨ Q (b i) = -1)
    (p : Finset I × ℤˣ) :
    ∃ u : monomialGroup Q b,
      ((u : (CliffordAlgebra Q)ˣ) : CliffordAlgebra Q) = (p.2 : ℤ) • basis Q b p.1 := by
  obtain ⟨u, hu⟩ := exists_monomialGroup_val_eq_basis hb hQ p.1
  rcases Int.units_eq_one_or p.2 with h | h
  · exact ⟨u, by simp [h, hu]⟩
  · exact ⟨monomialGroupEpsilon Q b * u, by simp [h, hu]⟩

/-- **The signed monomials, parametrized by support and sign**: for an orthogonal basis whose
generators square to `±1`, over a nontrivial ring in which `2` is invertible, `(s, ε) ↦ ε • e_s` is
a bijection from the pairs of a finite index set and a sign onto the group of signed monomials
(`CliffordAlgebra.coe_monomialGroupEquiv_apply`). -/
noncomputable def monomialGroupEquiv [Nontrivial R]
    (hb : (QuadraticMap.associated Q).IsOrthoᵢ b) (hQ : ∀ i, Q (b i) = 1 ∨ Q (b i) = -1) :
    Finset I × ℤˣ ≃ monomialGroup Q b :=
  Equiv.ofBijective (fun p ↦ (exists_monomialGroup_val_eq_zsmul_basis hb hQ p).choose) <| by
    have hval (p : Finset I × ℤˣ) :=
      (exists_monomialGroup_val_eq_zsmul_basis hb hQ p).choose_spec
    refine ⟨fun ⟨s, ε⟩ ⟨t, ε'⟩ hst ↦ ?_, fun u ↦ ?_⟩
    · -- The basis vectors are independent, and `e_s ≠ -e_t`.
      have h := congrArg (fun u : monomialGroup Q b ↦
        ((u : (CliffordAlgebra Q)ˣ) : CliffordAlgebra Q)) hst
      rw [hval, hval] at h
      rcases Int.units_eq_one_or ε with rfl | rfl <;>
        rcases Int.units_eq_one_or ε' with rfl | rfl <;>
        simp only [Units.val_one, Units.val_neg, one_smul, neg_smul, neg_inj] at h
      · rw [(basis Q b).injective h]
      · exact ((basis Q b).ne_neg (Invertible.ne_zero 2) s t h).elim
      · exact ((basis Q b).ne_neg (Invertible.ne_zero 2) t s h.symm).elim
      · rw [(basis Q b).injective h]
    · obtain ⟨s, hs | hs⟩ := (mem_monomialGroup_iff hb hQ).mp u.2
      · exact ⟨(s, 1), Subtype.ext (Units.ext (by rw [hval, hs, Units.val_one, one_smul]))⟩
      · exact ⟨(s, -1), Subtype.ext (Units.ext (by rw [hval, hs, Units.val_neg, Units.val_one,
          neg_one_smul]))⟩

/-- `CliffordAlgebra.monomialGroupEquiv` sends a finite index set `s` and a sign `ε` to the signed
monomial `ε • e_s`. -/
@[simp]
theorem coe_monomialGroupEquiv_apply [Nontrivial R]
    (hb : (QuadraticMap.associated Q).IsOrthoᵢ b) (hQ : ∀ i, Q (b i) = 1 ∨ Q (b i) = -1)
    (p : Finset I × ℤˣ) :
    ((monomialGroupEquiv hb hQ p : (CliffordAlgebra Q)ˣ) : CliffordAlgebra Q) =
      (p.2 : ℤ) • basis Q b p.1 :=
  (exists_monomialGroup_val_eq_zsmul_basis hb hQ p).choose_spec

/-- **The order of the group of signed monomials**: for an orthogonal basis over a nontrivial ring
in which `2` is invertible, indexed by a type with `n` elements and whose generators square to `±1`,
the group has `2 ^ (n + 1)` elements, the `±e_s` for the `2 ^ n` index sets `s`. -/
theorem natCard_monomialGroup [Fintype I] [Nontrivial R]
    (hb : (QuadraticMap.associated Q).IsOrthoᵢ b) (hQ : ∀ i, Q (b i) = 1 ∨ Q (b i) = -1) :
    Nat.card (monomialGroup Q b) = 2 ^ (Fintype.card I + 1) := by
  rw [← Nat.card_congr (monomialGroupEquiv hb hQ)]
  simp [Nat.card_eq_fintype_card, Fintype.card_finset, pow_succ]

/-- A signed basis monomial is central in the finite monomial subgroup exactly when its support is
empty, or when it is the full index set of odd cardinality, for an orthogonal basis whose vectors
square to `±1` over a nontrivial commutative ring in which `2` is invertible. -/
theorem mem_center_monomialGroup_iff [Fintype I] [Nontrivial R]
    (hb : (QuadraticMap.associated Q).IsOrthoᵢ b)
    (hQ : ∀ i, Q (b i) = 1 ∨ Q (b i) = -1)
    {u : monomialGroup Q b} :
    u ∈ Subgroup.center (monomialGroup Q b) ↔
      ∃ s : Finset I,
        ((↑(u : (CliffordAlgebra Q)ˣ) : CliffordAlgebra Q) = basis Q b s ∨
          (↑(u : (CliffordAlgebra Q)ˣ) : CliffordAlgebra Q) = -basis Q b s) ∧
        (s = ∅ ∨ (s = Finset.univ ∧ Odd s.card)) := by
  have central_comm_of_value (hu : u ∈ Subgroup.center (monomialGroup Q b))
      (s : Finset I) (hs : (↑(u : (CliffordAlgebra Q)ˣ) : CliffordAlgebra Q) = basis Q b s ∨
        (↑(u : (CliffordAlgebra Q)ˣ) : CliffordAlgebra Q) = -basis Q b s) :
      ∀ i : I, basis Q b s * ι Q (b i) = ι Q (b i) * basis Q b s := by
    intro i
    have hi : IsUnit (Q (b i)) := isUnit_of_eq_one_or_neg_one b hQ i
    obtain ⟨g, hg⟩ := exists_monomialGroup_val_eq_ι b hi
    have hc := Subgroup.mem_center_iff.mp hu g
    have hc' : (u : (CliffordAlgebra Q)ˣ) * (g : (CliffordAlgebra Q)ˣ) =
        (g : (CliffordAlgebra Q)ˣ) * (u : (CliffordAlgebra Q)ˣ) := by
      simpa using congrArg Subtype.val hc.symm
    have hc'' := congrArg Units.val hc'
    rcases hs with hs | hs
    · simpa [hs, hg] using hc''
    · simpa [hs, hg] using hc''
  constructor
  · intro hu
    obtain ⟨s, hs⟩ := (mem_monomialGroup_iff (b := b) hb hQ).mp u.property
    exact ⟨s, hs, (basis_comm_ι_iff hb (isUnit_of_eq_one_or_neg_one b hQ) s).mp
      (central_comm_of_value hu s hs)⟩
  · rintro ⟨s, hs, hpar⟩
    have hcenter : basis Q b s ∈ Subalgebra.center R (CliffordAlgebra Q) := by
      rcases hpar with rfl | ⟨rfl, hodd⟩
      · rw [basis_empty]
        exact one_mem _
      · exact basis_univ_mem_center_of_odd_card hb (by simpa using hodd)
    have hcomm_basis (x : CliffordAlgebra Q) :
        x * basis Q b s = basis Q b s * x :=
      Subalgebra.mem_center_iff.mp hcenter x
    rw [Subgroup.mem_center_iff]
    intro g
    apply Subtype.ext
    apply Units.ext
    rcases hs with hs | hs
    · simpa only [Subgroup.coe_mul, Units.val_mul, hs] using
        hcomm_basis ((g : (CliffordAlgebra Q)ˣ) : CliffordAlgebra Q)
    · simpa only [Subgroup.coe_mul, Units.val_mul, hs, mul_neg, neg_mul] using
        congrArg Neg.neg (hcomm_basis ((g : (CliffordAlgebra Q)ˣ) : CliffordAlgebra Q))

/-- **The group of signed monomials of a finite orthogonal basis is finite.** -/
theorem finite_monomialGroup [Finite I] [Nontrivial R]
    (hb : (QuadraticMap.associated Q).IsOrthoᵢ b) (hQ : ∀ i, Q (b i) = 1 ∨ Q (b i) = -1) :
    Finite (monomialGroup Q b) := by
  have : Fintype I := Fintype.ofFinite I
  have h : Nat.card (monomialGroup Q b) ≠ 0 := by
    rw [natCard_monomialGroup hb hQ]
    positivity
  exact (Nat.card_ne_zero.mp h).2

/-! ### The quotient by the sign subgroup of an orthogonal basis -/

/-- **The quotient by the sign subgroup has `2 ^ n` elements**, one for each of the `2 ^ n` index
sets: the group of signed monomials has `2 ^ (n + 1)` elements and the sign subgroup has two. -/
theorem natCard_quotient_monomialGroupSign [Fintype I] [Nontrivial R]
    (hb : (QuadraticMap.associated Q).IsOrthoᵢ b) (hQ : ∀ i, Q (b i) = 1 ∨ Q (b i) = -1) :
    Nat.card (monomialGroup Q b ⧸ monomialGroupSign Q b) = 2 ^ Fintype.card I := by
  have h := (monomialGroupSign Q b).card_eq_card_quotient_mul_card_subgroup
  rw [natCard_monomialGroup hb hQ, natCard_monomialGroupSign b two_ne_zero, pow_succ] at h
  exact (Nat.eq_of_mul_eq_mul_right two_pos h).symm

/-! ### The Clifford algebra as a quotient of the group algebra -/

/-- **The kernel of the group algebra map is generated by `ε + 1`**: for an orthogonal basis whose
generators square to `±1`, an element of the group algebra of the group of signed monomials maps to
zero in the Clifford algebra exactly when it is a multiple of `ε + 1`, for `ε = -1`. -/
theorem ker_monomialGroupAlgHom (hb : (QuadraticMap.associated Q).IsOrthoᵢ b)
    (hQ : ∀ i, Q (b i) = 1 ∨ Q (b i) = -1) :
    RingHom.ker (monomialGroupAlgHom Q b) =
      Ideal.span
        {MonoidAlgebra.of R (monomialGroup Q b) (monomialGroupEpsilon Q b) + 1} := by
  set x := MonoidAlgebra.of R (monomialGroup Q b) (monomialGroupEpsilon Q b) + 1 with hx
  refine le_antisymm (fun y hy ↦ ?_) (Ideal.span_le.mpr (Set.singleton_subset_iff.mpr
    (monomialGroupAlgHom_of_monomialGroupEpsilon_add_one_eq_zero b)))
  -- Every basis vector `e_s` is the value of a group element `u s`.
  choose u hu using exists_monomialGroup_val_eq_basis hb hQ
  -- Lifting `e_s` back to `u s` is a linear section of the group algebra map, modulo `ε + 1`.
  let ψ : CliffordAlgebra Q →ₗ[R] MonoidAlgebra R (monomialGroup Q b) :=
    (basis Q b).constr R fun s ↦ MonoidAlgebra.of R _ (u s)
  have key (z : MonoidAlgebra R (monomialGroup Q b)) :
      z - ψ (monomialGroupAlgHom Q b z) ∈ Ideal.span {x} := by
    induction z using MonoidAlgebra.induction_on with
    | of g =>
      obtain ⟨s, hs | hs⟩ := (mem_monomialGroup_iff hb hQ).mp g.2
      · obtain rfl : g = u s := Subtype.ext (Units.ext (hs.trans (hu s).symm))
        rw [monomialGroupAlgHom_of, hu, Module.Basis.constr_basis, sub_self]
        exact zero_mem _
      · -- Here `g = ε * u s`, and `of g + of (u s) = of (u s) * (ε + 1)`.
        have hg : g = monomialGroupEpsilon Q b * u s :=
          Subtype.ext (Units.ext (by simp [hs, hu]))
        have hmem : MonoidAlgebra.of R _ (u s) * x ∈ Ideal.span {x} :=
          Ideal.mul_mem_left _ _ (Ideal.mem_span_singleton_self x)
        convert hmem using 1
        rw [monomialGroupAlgHom_of, hs, map_neg, Module.Basis.constr_basis, sub_neg_eq_add, hg,
          of_monomialGroupEpsilon_mul_add_of]
    | add y z hy hz => simpa [add_sub_add_comm] using add_mem hy hz
    | smul r y hy => simpa [smul_sub] using Submodule.smul_of_tower_mem _ r hy
  simpa [RingHom.mem_ker.mp hy] using key y

/-- **The Clifford algebra is the group algebra of the group of signed monomials modulo
`ε + 1`**: for an orthogonal basis whose generators square to `±1`, the class of a group element
maps to its value. -/
noncomputable def monomialGroupAlgebraQuotientEquiv (hb : (QuadraticMap.associated Q).IsOrthoᵢ b)
    (hQ : ∀ i, Q (b i) = 1 ∨ Q (b i) = -1) :
    (MonoidAlgebra R (monomialGroup Q b) ⧸
      Ideal.span {MonoidAlgebra.of R (monomialGroup Q b) (monomialGroupEpsilon Q b) + 1})
      ≃ₐ[R] CliffordAlgebra Q :=
  (Ideal.quotientEquivAlgOfEq R (ker_monomialGroupAlgHom hb hQ).symm).trans
    (Ideal.quotientKerAlgEquivOfSurjective (monomialGroupAlgHom_surjective b b.span_eq
      (isUnit_of_eq_one_or_neg_one b hQ)))

/-- `CliffordAlgebra.monomialGroupAlgebraQuotientEquiv` sends the class of `z` to its image under
`CliffordAlgebra.monomialGroupAlgHom`. -/
@[simp]
theorem monomialGroupAlgebraQuotientEquiv_mk (hb : (QuadraticMap.associated Q).IsOrthoᵢ b)
    (hQ : ∀ i, Q (b i) = 1 ∨ Q (b i) = -1) (z : MonoidAlgebra R (monomialGroup Q b)) :
    monomialGroupAlgebraQuotientEquiv hb hQ (Ideal.Quotient.mk _ z) =
      monomialGroupAlgHom Q b z := by
  simp [monomialGroupAlgebraQuotientEquiv]

/-- The inverse of `CliffordAlgebra.monomialGroupAlgebraQuotientEquiv` sends the value of a group
element to its class. -/
@[simp]
theorem monomialGroupAlgebraQuotientEquiv_symm_apply_coe
    (hb : (QuadraticMap.associated Q).IsOrthoᵢ b) (hQ : ∀ i, Q (b i) = 1 ∨ Q (b i) = -1)
    (g : monomialGroup Q b) :
    (monomialGroupAlgebraQuotientEquiv hb hQ).symm
        ((g : (CliffordAlgebra Q)ˣ) : CliffordAlgebra Q) =
      Ideal.Quotient.mk _ (MonoidAlgebra.of R (monomialGroup Q b) g) := by
  rw [AlgEquiv.symm_apply_eq, monomialGroupAlgebraQuotientEquiv_mk, monomialGroupAlgHom_of]

/-- The algebra map from the Clifford algebra induced by a monoid map from the group of signed
monomials sending `ε` to `-1`; it is `CliffordAlgebra.monomialGroupLift`. -/
private noncomputable def monomialGroupLiftAux (hb : (QuadraticMap.associated Q).IsOrthoᵢ b)
    (hQ : ∀ i, Q (b i) = 1 ∨ Q (b i) = -1) {A : Type*} [Ring A] [Algebra R A]
    (f : {f : monomialGroup Q b →* A // f (monomialGroupEpsilon Q b) = -1}) :
    CliffordAlgebra Q →ₐ[R] A :=
  (Ideal.Quotient.liftₐ _ (MonoidAlgebra.lift R A _ f) fun _ hz ↦
      RingHom.mem_ker.mp ((Ideal.span_le.mpr (Set.singleton_subset_iff.mpr
        (by simp [RingHom.mem_ker, f.2]))) hz)).comp
    (monomialGroupAlgebraQuotientEquiv hb hQ).symm.toAlgHom

/-- `CliffordAlgebra.monomialGroupLiftAux hb hQ f` sends the value of `g` to `f g`. -/
private theorem monomialGroupLiftAux_apply_coe (hb : (QuadraticMap.associated Q).IsOrthoᵢ b)
    (hQ : ∀ i, Q (b i) = 1 ∨ Q (b i) = -1) {A : Type*} [Ring A] [Algebra R A]
    (f : {f : monomialGroup Q b →* A // f (monomialGroupEpsilon Q b) = -1})
    (g : monomialGroup Q b) :
    monomialGroupLiftAux hb hQ f ((g : (CliffordAlgebra Q)ˣ) : CliffordAlgebra Q) = f.1 g := by
  simp only [monomialGroupLiftAux, AlgHom.comp_apply, AlgEquiv.coe_toAlgHom,
    monomialGroupAlgebraQuotientEquiv_symm_apply_coe]
  exact MonoidAlgebra.lift_of ..

/-- **The universal property of the Clifford algebra in terms of its signed monomials**: for an
orthogonal basis whose generators square to `±1`, algebra maps from the Clifford algebra to an
`R`-algebra `A` are the same as monoid maps from the group of signed monomials to `A` sending
`ε = -1` to `-1`. For `A = Module.End R W` this identifies the Clifford module structures on `W`
with the representations of the group on `W` in which `ε` acts by `-1`. -/
noncomputable def monomialGroupLift (hb : (QuadraticMap.associated Q).IsOrthoᵢ b)
    (hQ : ∀ i, Q (b i) = 1 ∨ Q (b i) = -1) {A : Type*} [Ring A] [Algebra R A] :
    {f : monomialGroup Q b →* A // f (monomialGroupEpsilon Q b) = -1} ≃
      (CliffordAlgebra Q →ₐ[R] A) where
  toFun := monomialGroupLiftAux hb hQ
  invFun F := ⟨(F : CliffordAlgebra Q →* A).comp
      ((Units.coeHom (CliffordAlgebra Q)).comp (monomialGroup Q b).subtype), by simp⟩
  left_inv f := Subtype.ext <| MonoidHom.ext fun g ↦ monomialGroupLiftAux_apply_coe hb hQ f g
  right_inv F := by
    refine hom_ext (b.ext fun i ↦ ?_)
    obtain ⟨g, hg⟩ := exists_monomialGroup_val_eq_ι b (isUnit_of_eq_one_or_neg_one b hQ i)
    have := monomialGroupLiftAux_apply_coe hb hQ ⟨(F : CliffordAlgebra Q →* A).comp
      ((Units.coeHom (CliffordAlgebra Q)).comp (monomialGroup Q b).subtype), by simp⟩ g
    simpa [hg] using this

/-- The algebra map `CliffordAlgebra.monomialGroupLift hb hQ f` sends the value of each group
element `g` to `f g`. -/
@[simp]
theorem monomialGroupLift_apply_coe (hb : (QuadraticMap.associated Q).IsOrthoᵢ b)
    (hQ : ∀ i, Q (b i) = 1 ∨ Q (b i) = -1) {A : Type*} [Ring A] [Algebra R A]
    (f : {f : monomialGroup Q b →* A // f (monomialGroupEpsilon Q b) = -1})
    (g : monomialGroup Q b) :
    monomialGroupLift hb hQ f ((g : (CliffordAlgebra Q)ˣ) : CliffordAlgebra Q) = f.1 g :=
  monomialGroupLiftAux_apply_coe hb hQ f g

/-- The monoid map attached by `CliffordAlgebra.monomialGroupLift` to an algebra map `F` from the
Clifford algebra is `F` applied to the values of the group elements. -/
@[simp]
theorem monomialGroupLift_symm_apply_coe (hb : (QuadraticMap.associated Q).IsOrthoᵢ b)
    (hQ : ∀ i, Q (b i) = 1 ∨ Q (b i) = -1) {A : Type*} [Ring A] [Algebra R A]
    (F : CliffordAlgebra Q →ₐ[R] A) (g : monomialGroup Q b) :
    ((monomialGroupLift hb hQ).symm F).1 g = F ((g : (CliffordAlgebra Q)ˣ) : CliffordAlgebra Q) :=
  (rfl)

/-! ### Conjugacy classes -/

omit [Invertible (2 : R)] [LinearOrder I] in
/-- **A noncentral signed monomial is conjugate exactly to itself and its negative**: for pairwise
orthogonal vectors, a signed monomial `u` that is not central anticommutes with some signed
monomial `g`, and conjugation by `g` sends it to `-u`. -/
theorem monomialGroup_isConj_iff_of_notMem_center
    (v : I → M) (hv : ∀ i j, i ≠ j → Q.IsOrtho (v i) (v j))
    {u w : monomialGroup Q v} (hu : u ∉ Subgroup.center (monomialGroup Q v)) :
    IsConj u w ↔ (w : (CliffordAlgebra Q)ˣ) = (u : (CliffordAlgebra Q)ˣ) ∨
      (w : (CliffordAlgebra Q)ˣ) = -(u : (CliffordAlgebra Q)ˣ) := by
  refine ⟨monomialGroup_val_eq_or_neg_of_isConj v hv, ?_⟩
  rintro (hw | hw)
  · rw [Subtype.ext hw]
  · obtain ⟨g, hg⟩ : ∃ g, g * u ≠ u * g := by
      simpa [Subgroup.mem_center_iff] using hu
    rcases (monomialGroup_commuteOrNeg v hv g u).out with hc | hc
    · exact (hg (Subtype.ext hc.eq)).elim
    · refine isConj_iff.mpr ⟨g, Subtype.ext ?_⟩
      simp only [Subgroup.coe_mul, Subgroup.coe_inv, hw, hc.eq, neg_mul, mul_inv_cancel_right]

omit [Invertible (2 : R)] [LinearOrder I] in
/-- **A noncentral conjugacy class of signed monomials has two elements**, `u` and `-u`, for
pairwise orthogonal vectors. -/
theorem natCard_carrier_monomialGroup_of_notMem_center
    (v : I → M) (hv : ∀ i j, i ≠ j → Q.IsOrtho (v i) (v j))
    {u : monomialGroup Q v} (hu : u ∉ Subgroup.center (monomialGroup Q v)) :
    Nat.card (ConjClasses.mk u).carrier = 2 := by
  set ε : monomialGroup Q v := monomialGroupEpsilon Q v
  have hcarrier : (ConjClasses.mk u).carrier = {u, ε * u} := by
    ext w
    rw [ConjClasses.mem_carrier_iff_mk_eq, ConjClasses.mk_eq_mk_iff_isConj, isConj_comm,
      monomialGroup_isConj_iff_of_notMem_center v hv hu, Set.mem_insert_iff,
      Set.mem_singleton_iff, Subtype.ext_iff, Subtype.ext_iff, Subgroup.coe_mul]
    simp only [ε, coe_monomialGroupEpsilon, neg_one_mul]
  -- `u ≠ -u`: otherwise anticommuting with `u` would be commuting with it, so `u` would be central.
  have hne : u ≠ ε * u := by
    intro h
    have hneg : -(u : (CliffordAlgebra Q)ˣ) = u := by
      have h' := congrArg (fun g : monomialGroup Q v ↦ (g : (CliffordAlgebra Q)ˣ)) h
      simp only [Subgroup.coe_mul, ε, coe_monomialGroupEpsilon, neg_one_mul] at h'
      exact h'.symm
    refine hu (Subgroup.mem_center_iff.mpr fun g ↦ Subtype.ext ?_)
    rcases (monomialGroup_commuteOrNeg v hv g u).out with hc | hc
    · exact hc.eq
    · simpa only [Subgroup.coe_mul, hneg] using hc.eq
  rw [hcarrier, Nat.card_coe_set_eq, Set.ncard_pair hne]

variable [Nontrivial R] [Fintype I]

/-- A signed monomial `ε • e_s` is central exactly when its support `s` is empty or is the full
index set of odd cardinality. -/
@[simp]
theorem monomialGroupEquiv_mem_center_iff
    (hb : (QuadraticMap.associated Q).IsOrthoᵢ b) (hQ : ∀ i, Q (b i) = 1 ∨ Q (b i) = -1)
    (p : Finset I × ℤˣ) :
    monomialGroupEquiv hb hQ p ∈ Subgroup.center (monomialGroup Q b) ↔
      p.1 = ∅ ∨ (p.1 = Finset.univ ∧ Odd p.1.card) := by
  rw [mem_center_monomialGroup_iff hb hQ, coe_monomialGroupEquiv_apply]
  constructor
  · rintro ⟨s, hs, hc⟩
    -- The support of `ε • e_{p.1} = ±e_s` is `s`.
    suffices p.1 = s by rwa [this]
    rcases hs with hs | hs
    · exact congrArg Prod.fst ((monomialGroupEquiv hb hQ).injective (a₂ := (s, 1))
        (Subtype.ext (Units.ext (by
          rw [coe_monomialGroupEquiv_apply, coe_monomialGroupEquiv_apply, hs, Units.val_one,
            one_smul]))))
    · exact congrArg Prod.fst ((monomialGroupEquiv hb hQ).injective (a₂ := (s, -1))
        (Subtype.ext (Units.ext (by
          rw [coe_monomialGroupEquiv_apply, coe_monomialGroupEquiv_apply, hs, Units.val_neg,
            Units.val_one, neg_one_smul]))))
  · intro hc
    refine ⟨p.1, ?_, hc⟩
    rcases Int.units_eq_one_or p.2 with h | h <;> simp [h]

/-- The centre of the group of signed monomials has two elements for each of its supports: the
empty set and, in odd dimension, the full index set. -/
private theorem natCard_center_monomialGroup
    (hb : (QuadraticMap.associated Q).IsOrthoᵢ b) (hQ : ∀ i, Q (b i) = 1 ∨ Q (b i) = -1) :
    Nat.card (Subgroup.center (monomialGroup Q b)) =
      Nat.card {s : Finset I // s = ∅ ∨ (s = Finset.univ ∧ Odd s.card)} * 2 := by
  have e : Subgroup.center (monomialGroup Q b) ≃
      {s : Finset I // s = ∅ ∨ (s = Finset.univ ∧ Odd s.card)} × ℤˣ :=
    ((monomialGroupEquiv hb hQ).subtypeEquiv
      (p := fun p ↦ p.1 = ∅ ∨ (p.1 = Finset.univ ∧ Odd p.1.card))
      (q := (· ∈ Subgroup.center (monomialGroup Q b)))
      fun p ↦ (monomialGroupEquiv_mem_center_iff hb hQ p).symm).symm.trans
      (Equiv.prodSubtypeFstEquivSubtypeProd (β := ℤˣ)
        (p := fun s : Finset I ↦ s = ∅ ∨ (s = Finset.univ ∧ Odd s.card)))
  rw [Nat.card_congr e, Nat.card_prod]
  simp [Nat.card_eq_fintype_card]

/-- **The centre of the group of signed monomials in even dimension** has two elements, `1` and
`ε = -1`, for an orthogonal basis whose generators square to `±1`, indexed by a type of even
cardinality. -/
theorem natCard_center_monomialGroup_of_even
    (hb : (QuadraticMap.associated Q).IsOrthoᵢ b) (hQ : ∀ i, Q (b i) = 1 ∨ Q (b i) = -1)
    (hn : Even (Fintype.card I)) :
    Nat.card (Subgroup.center (monomialGroup Q b)) = 2 := by
  -- The full index set has even cardinality, so only the empty support is central.
  have hsupp (s : Finset I) : (s = ∅ ∨ (s = Finset.univ ∧ Odd s.card)) ↔ s = ∅ :=
    or_iff_left fun ⟨hs, hodd⟩ ↦
      Nat.not_odd_iff_even.mpr hn (by rwa [hs, Finset.card_univ] at hodd)
  rw [natCard_center_monomialGroup hb hQ, Nat.card_congr (Equiv.subtypeEquivRight hsupp)]
  simp

/-- **The centre of the group of signed monomials in odd dimension** has four elements, `±1` and
`±ω` for `ω = e_univ` the volume element, for an orthogonal basis whose generators square to `±1`,
indexed by a type of odd cardinality. -/
theorem natCard_center_monomialGroup_of_odd
    (hb : (QuadraticMap.associated Q).IsOrthoᵢ b) (hQ : ∀ i, Q (b i) = 1 ∨ Q (b i) = -1)
    (hn : Odd (Fintype.card I)) :
    Nat.card (Subgroup.center (monomialGroup Q b)) = 4 := by
  have hsupp (s : Finset I) : (s = ∅ ∨ (s = Finset.univ ∧ Odd s.card)) ↔
      s ∈ ({∅, Finset.univ} : Finset (Finset I)) := by
    rw [Finset.mem_insert, Finset.mem_singleton]
    exact or_congr_right ⟨And.left, fun hs ↦ ⟨hs, by rwa [hs, Finset.card_univ]⟩⟩
  -- The index type is nonempty, so the two central supports differ.
  have hne : (∅ : Finset I) ≠ Finset.univ :=
    (Finset.univ_nonempty_iff.mpr (Fintype.card_pos_iff.mp hn.pos)).ne_empty.symm
  rw [natCard_center_monomialGroup hb hQ, Nat.card_congr (Equiv.subtypeEquivRight hsupp),
    Nat.card_eq_fintype_card, Fintype.card_coe, Finset.card_pair hne]

/-- Twice the number of conjugacy classes of the group of signed monomials is the order of the
group plus the order of its centre, since every noncentral class has two elements. -/
private theorem two_mul_natCard_conjClasses_monomialGroup
    (hb : (QuadraticMap.associated Q).IsOrthoᵢ b) (hQ : ∀ i, Q (b i) = 1 ∨ Q (b i) = -1) :
    2 * Nat.card (ConjClasses (monomialGroup Q b)) =
      2 ^ (Fintype.card I + 1) + Nat.card (Subgroup.center (monomialGroup Q b)) := by
  have := Finite.of_equiv _ (monomialGroupEquiv hb hQ)
  rw [← natCard_monomialGroup hb hQ]
  refine TauCeti.ConjClasses.two_mul_natCard_eq_of_forall_noncenter fun C hC ↦ ?_
  obtain ⟨u, rfl⟩ := C.exists_rep
  exact natCard_carrier_monomialGroup_of_notMem_center b
    (fun _ _ hij ↦ QuadraticMap.associated_isOrtho.mp (hb hij))
    fun hu ↦ (ConjClasses.mk_bijOn _).mapsTo hu hC

/-- **The number of conjugacy classes of the group of signed monomials in even dimension**: for an
orthogonal basis of `n` vectors, `n` even, whose generators square to `±1`, the group has
`2 ^ n + 1` conjugacy classes, its two central elements and the `2 ^ n - 1` pairs `{u, -u}`. -/
theorem natCard_conjClasses_monomialGroup_of_even
    (hb : (QuadraticMap.associated Q).IsOrthoᵢ b) (hQ : ∀ i, Q (b i) = 1 ∨ Q (b i) = -1)
    (hn : Even (Fintype.card I)) :
    Nat.card (ConjClasses (monomialGroup Q b)) = 2 ^ Fintype.card I + 1 := by
  have h := two_mul_natCard_conjClasses_monomialGroup hb hQ
  rw [natCard_center_monomialGroup_of_even hb hQ hn, pow_succ] at h
  omega

/-- **The number of conjugacy classes of the group of signed monomials in odd dimension**: for an
orthogonal basis of `n` vectors, `n` odd, whose generators square to `±1`, the group has
`2 ^ n + 2` conjugacy classes, its four central elements and the `2 ^ n - 2` pairs `{u, -u}`. -/
theorem natCard_conjClasses_monomialGroup_of_odd
    (hb : (QuadraticMap.associated Q).IsOrthoᵢ b) (hQ : ∀ i, Q (b i) = 1 ∨ Q (b i) = -1)
    (hn : Odd (Fintype.card I)) :
    Nat.card (ConjClasses (monomialGroup Q b)) = 2 ^ Fintype.card I + 2 := by
  have h := two_mul_natCard_conjClasses_monomialGroup hb hQ
  rw [natCard_center_monomialGroup_of_odd hb hQ hn, pow_succ] at h
  omega

/-! ### The support homomorphism and the characters trivial on `ε` -/

omit [Fintype I] in
/-- The support of a signed monomial `±e_s`, read off its parametrization, is `s`. -/
private theorem monomialGroupEquiv_symm_fst_of_val_eq
    (hb : (QuadraticMap.associated Q).IsOrthoᵢ b) (hQ : ∀ i, Q (b i) = 1 ∨ Q (b i) = -1)
    {g : monomialGroup Q b} {s : Finset I}
    (hg : ((g : (CliffordAlgebra Q)ˣ) : CliffordAlgebra Q) = basis Q b s ∨
      ((g : (CliffordAlgebra Q)ˣ) : CliffordAlgebra Q) = -basis Q b s) :
    ((monomialGroupEquiv hb hQ).symm g).1 = s := by
  obtain ⟨e, he⟩ : ∃ e : ℤˣ, monomialGroupEquiv hb hQ (s, e) = g := by
    rcases hg with hg | hg
    · exact ⟨1, Subtype.ext (Units.ext (by simp [hg]))⟩
    · exact ⟨-1, Subtype.ext (Units.ext (by simp [hg]))⟩
  rw [← he, Equiv.symm_apply_apply]

omit [Nontrivial R] [Fintype I] in
/-- The product of signed monomials `±e_s` and `±e_t` is a signed monomial `±e_{s ∆ t}`. -/
private theorem val_mul_eq_or_of_val_eq_or (hb : (QuadraticMap.associated Q).IsOrthoᵢ b)
    (hQ : ∀ i, Q (b i) = 1 ∨ Q (b i) = -1) {g h : monomialGroup Q b} {s t : Finset I}
    (hs : ((g : (CliffordAlgebra Q)ˣ) : CliffordAlgebra Q) = basis Q b s ∨
      ((g : (CliffordAlgebra Q)ˣ) : CliffordAlgebra Q) = -basis Q b s)
    (ht : ((h : (CliffordAlgebra Q)ˣ) : CliffordAlgebra Q) = basis Q b t ∨
      ((h : (CliffordAlgebra Q)ˣ) : CliffordAlgebra Q) = -basis Q b t) :
    (((g * h : monomialGroup Q b) : (CliffordAlgebra Q)ˣ) : CliffordAlgebra Q) =
        basis Q b (s ∆ t) ∨
      (((g * h : monomialGroup Q b) : (CliffordAlgebra Q)ˣ) : CliffordAlgebra Q) =
        -basis Q b (s ∆ t) := by
  rw [Subgroup.coe_mul, Units.val_mul]
  rcases basis_mul_basis_eq_or hb hQ s t with hst | hst <;>
    rcases hs with hs | hs <;> rcases ht with ht | ht <;>
    simp only [hs, ht, neg_mul, mul_neg, neg_neg, hst, true_or, or_true]

omit [Fintype I] in
/-- **The support homomorphism.** For an orthogonal basis whose generators square to `±1`, the
signed monomial `±e_s` is sent to the indicator vector of `s` in `(ZMod 2) ^ I`, written
multiplicatively. It is a homomorphism because `e_s * e_t = ±e_{s ∆ t}`; it is onto when `I` is
finite (`CliffordAlgebra.monomialGroupSupport_surjective`), with kernel `{1, ε}` for `ε = -1`
(`CliffordAlgebra.ker_monomialGroupSupport`), so it identifies the quotient by `ε` with the
elementary abelian `2`-group `(ZMod 2) ^ I`. -/
noncomputable def monomialGroupSupport (hb : (QuadraticMap.associated Q).IsOrthoᵢ b)
    (hQ : ∀ i, Q (b i) = 1 ∨ Q (b i) = -1) :
    monomialGroup Q b →* Multiplicative (I → ZMod 2) where
  toFun g := .ofAdd ((((monomialGroupEquiv hb hQ).symm g).1 : Set I).indicator 1)
  map_one' := by
    rw [monomialGroupEquiv_symm_fst_of_val_eq hb hQ (s := ∅) (Or.inl (by simp)),
      Finset.coe_empty, Set.indicator_empty', ofAdd_zero]
  map_mul' g h := by
    obtain ⟨s, hs⟩ := (mem_monomialGroup_iff hb hQ).mp g.2
    obtain ⟨t, ht⟩ := (mem_monomialGroup_iff hb hQ).mp h.2
    rw [monomialGroupEquiv_symm_fst_of_val_eq hb hQ (val_mul_eq_or_of_val_eq_or hb hQ hs ht),
      monomialGroupEquiv_symm_fst_of_val_eq hb hQ hs,
      monomialGroupEquiv_symm_fst_of_val_eq hb hQ ht, ← ofAdd_add]
    classical
    congr 1
    ext i
    by_cases his : i ∈ s <;> by_cases hit : i ∈ t <;>
      simp [Set.mem_symmDiff, his, hit, CharTwo.add_self_eq_zero]

omit [Fintype I] in
/-- The support of a signed monomial `±e_s` is the indicator vector of `s`. -/
theorem monomialGroupSupport_apply_of_val_eq (hb : (QuadraticMap.associated Q).IsOrthoᵢ b)
    (hQ : ∀ i, Q (b i) = 1 ∨ Q (b i) = -1) {g : monomialGroup Q b} {s : Finset I}
    (hg : ((g : (CliffordAlgebra Q)ˣ) : CliffordAlgebra Q) = basis Q b s ∨
      ((g : (CliffordAlgebra Q)ˣ) : CliffordAlgebra Q) = -basis Q b s) :
    monomialGroupSupport hb hQ g = .ofAdd ((s : Set I).indicator 1) := by
  simp only [monomialGroupSupport, MonoidHom.coe_mk, OneHom.coe_mk,
    monomialGroupEquiv_symm_fst_of_val_eq hb hQ hg]

omit [Fintype I] in
/-- The support of the signed monomial `ε • e_s` is the indicator vector of `s`. -/
@[simp]
theorem monomialGroupSupport_monomialGroupEquiv (hb : (QuadraticMap.associated Q).IsOrthoᵢ b)
    (hQ : ∀ i, Q (b i) = 1 ∨ Q (b i) = -1) (p : Finset I × ℤˣ) :
    monomialGroupSupport hb hQ (monomialGroupEquiv hb hQ p) = .ofAdd ((p.1 : Set I).indicator 1) :=
  monomialGroupSupport_apply_of_val_eq hb hQ <| by
    rcases Int.units_eq_one_or p.2 with h | h <;> simp [h]

omit [Fintype I] in
/-- A signed monomial has trivial support exactly when it is `1` or `ε = -1`. -/
theorem monomialGroupSupport_eq_one_iff (hb : (QuadraticMap.associated Q).IsOrthoᵢ b)
    (hQ : ∀ i, Q (b i) = 1 ∨ Q (b i) = -1) {g : monomialGroup Q b} :
    monomialGroupSupport hb hQ g = 1 ↔ g = 1 ∨ g = monomialGroupEpsilon Q b := by
  obtain ⟨⟨s, e⟩, rfl⟩ := (monomialGroupEquiv hb hQ).surjective g
  have h1 : (1 : monomialGroup Q b) = monomialGroupEquiv hb hQ (∅, 1) :=
    Subtype.ext (Units.ext (by simp))
  have hε : monomialGroupEpsilon Q b = monomialGroupEquiv hb hQ (∅, -1) :=
    Subtype.ext (Units.ext (by simp))
  have hs : (s : Set I).indicator (1 : I → ZMod 2) = 0 ↔ s = ∅ := by
    classical
    rw [Finset.eq_empty_iff_forall_notMem, funext_iff]
    refine forall_congr' fun i ↦ ?_
    by_cases hi : i ∈ s <;> simp [hi]
  rw [h1, hε, (monomialGroupEquiv hb hQ).apply_eq_iff_eq,
    (monomialGroupEquiv hb hQ).apply_eq_iff_eq, monomialGroupSupport_monomialGroupEquiv,
    ← ofAdd_zero, EmbeddingLike.apply_eq_iff_eq, hs]
  rcases Int.units_eq_one_or e with rfl | rfl <;> simp

omit [Fintype I] in
/-- **The kernel of the support homomorphism** is the sign subgroup `{1, ε}`. -/
theorem ker_monomialGroupSupport (hb : (QuadraticMap.associated Q).IsOrthoᵢ b)
    (hQ : ∀ i, Q (b i) = 1 ∨ Q (b i) = -1) :
    (monomialGroupSupport hb hQ).ker = monomialGroupSign Q b :=
  Subgroup.ext fun _ ↦ by
    rw [MonoidHom.mem_ker, monomialGroupSupport_eq_one_iff, mem_monomialGroupSign_iff]

omit [Fintype I] in
/-- **The support homomorphism is onto** for a finite index type: the indicator vector of `s` is
the support of `e_s`. -/
theorem monomialGroupSupport_surjective [Finite I] (hb : (QuadraticMap.associated Q).IsOrthoᵢ b)
    (hQ : ∀ i, Q (b i) = 1 ∨ Q (b i) = -1) :
    Function.Surjective (monomialGroupSupport hb hQ) := by
  classical
  have := Fintype.ofFinite I
  intro x
  refine ⟨monomialGroupEquiv hb hQ (Finset.univ.filter fun i ↦ x.toAdd i = 1, 1), ?_⟩
  rw [monomialGroupSupport_monomialGroupEquiv]
  refine Multiplicative.toAdd.injective (funext fun i ↦ ?_)
  simp only [toAdd_ofAdd, Finset.coe_filter, Finset.mem_univ, true_and]
  by_cases hi : x.toAdd i = 1
  · simp [hi]
  · have hnot : i ∉ {i | x.toAdd i = 1} := hi
    have hbinary : ∀ a : ZMod 2, a = 0 ∨ a = 1 := by decide
    rw [Set.indicator_of_notMem hnot]
    exact ((hbinary _).resolve_right hi).symm

omit [Fintype I] in
/-- **The group of signed monomials modulo the sign subgroup is the elementary abelian group
`(ZMod 2) ^ I`**, for an orthogonal basis indexed by a finite type whose generators square to `±1`:
the class of a signed monomial is sent to its support. -/
noncomputable def monomialGroupQuotientEquiv [Finite I]
    (hb : (QuadraticMap.associated Q).IsOrthoᵢ b) (hQ : ∀ i, Q (b i) = 1 ∨ Q (b i) = -1) :
    monomialGroup Q b ⧸ monomialGroupSign Q b ≃* Multiplicative (I → ZMod 2) :=
  (QuotientGroup.quotientMulEquivOfEq (ker_monomialGroupSupport hb hQ).symm).trans
    (QuotientGroup.quotientKerEquivOfSurjective _ (monomialGroupSupport_surjective hb hQ))

omit [Fintype I] in
/-- `CliffordAlgebra.monomialGroupQuotientEquiv` sends the class of a signed monomial to its
support. -/
@[simp]
theorem monomialGroupQuotientEquiv_mk [Finite I] (hb : (QuadraticMap.associated Q).IsOrthoᵢ b)
    (hQ : ∀ i, Q (b i) = 1 ∨ Q (b i) = -1) (g : monomialGroup Q b) :
    monomialGroupQuotientEquiv hb hQ g = monomialGroupSupport hb hQ g :=
  (rfl)

omit [Fintype I] in
/-- **The sign characters trivial on `ε`.** For a finite index set `t`, the character of the group
of signed monomials sending `±e_s` to `(-1) ^ #(s ∩ t)`
(`CliffordAlgebra.monomialGroupCharacter_apply_of_val_eq`). It is the support homomorphism
followed by the character `x ↦ (-1) ^ ∑ i ∈ t, x i` of `(ZMod 2) ^ I`, so it is trivial on
`ε = -1`. For a finite index type these are all the characters trivial on `ε` with values in a
domain of characteristic not two (`CliffordAlgebra.existsUnique_monomialGroupCharacter_eq`). -/
noncomputable def monomialGroupCharacter (hb : (QuadraticMap.associated Q).IsOrthoᵢ b)
    (hQ : ∀ i, Q (b i) = 1 ∨ Q (b i) = -1) (t : Finset I) : monomialGroup Q b →* ℤˣ where
  toFun g := (-1) ^ ∑ i ∈ t, (monomialGroupSupport hb hQ g).toAdd i
  map_one' := by simp
  map_mul' g h := by simp [Finset.sum_add_distrib, uzpow_add]

omit [Fintype I] in
/-- The sign character `χ_t` sends a signed monomial `±e_s` to `(-1) ^ #(s ∩ t)`. -/
theorem monomialGroupCharacter_apply_of_val_eq (hb : (QuadraticMap.associated Q).IsOrthoᵢ b)
    (hQ : ∀ i, Q (b i) = 1 ∨ Q (b i) = -1) (t : Finset I) {g : monomialGroup Q b} {s : Finset I}
    (hg : ((g : (CliffordAlgebra Q)ˣ) : CliffordAlgebra Q) = basis Q b s ∨
      ((g : (CliffordAlgebra Q)ˣ) : CliffordAlgebra Q) = -basis Q b s) :
    monomialGroupCharacter hb hQ t g = (-1) ^ (s ∩ t).card := by
  simp only [monomialGroupCharacter, MonoidHom.coe_mk, OneHom.coe_mk,
    monomialGroupSupport_apply_of_val_eq hb hQ hg, toAdd_ofAdd, Set.indicator_apply,
    Finset.mem_coe, Pi.one_apply, Finset.sum_boole, Finset.filter_mem_eq_inter, uzpow_natCast]
  rw [Finset.inter_comm]

omit [Fintype I] in
/-- The sign character `χ_t` sends the signed monomial `ε • e_s` to `(-1) ^ #(s ∩ t)`. -/
@[simp]
theorem monomialGroupCharacter_monomialGroupEquiv (hb : (QuadraticMap.associated Q).IsOrthoᵢ b)
    (hQ : ∀ i, Q (b i) = 1 ∨ Q (b i) = -1) (t : Finset I) (p : Finset I × ℤˣ) :
    monomialGroupCharacter hb hQ t (monomialGroupEquiv hb hQ p) = (-1) ^ (p.1 ∩ t).card :=
  monomialGroupCharacter_apply_of_val_eq hb hQ t <| by
    rcases Int.units_eq_one_or p.2 with h | h <;> simp [h]

omit [Fintype I] in
/-- The sign characters are trivial on `ε = -1`. -/
@[simp]
theorem monomialGroupCharacter_monomialGroupEpsilon (hb : (QuadraticMap.associated Q).IsOrthoᵢ b)
    (hQ : ∀ i, Q (b i) = 1 ∨ Q (b i) = -1) (t : Finset I) :
    monomialGroupCharacter hb hQ t (monomialGroupEpsilon Q b) = 1 := by
  rw [monomialGroupCharacter_apply_of_val_eq hb hQ t (s := ∅) (Or.inr (by simp))]
  simp

omit [Fintype I] in
/-- Distinct index sets give distinct sign characters: `χ_t` takes the value `-1` at the
generator `e_i` exactly when `i ∈ t`. -/
theorem monomialGroupCharacter_injective (hb : (QuadraticMap.associated Q).IsOrthoᵢ b)
    (hQ : ∀ i, Q (b i) = 1 ∨ Q (b i) = -1) :
    Function.Injective (monomialGroupCharacter hb hQ) := by
  intro t t' h
  ext i
  obtain ⟨g, hg⟩ := exists_monomialGroup_val_eq_basis hb hQ {i}
  have hi := DFunLike.congr_fun h g
  rw [monomialGroupCharacter_apply_of_val_eq hb hQ t (Or.inl hg),
    monomialGroupCharacter_apply_of_val_eq hb hQ t' (Or.inl hg)] at hi
  by_cases hit : i ∈ t <;> by_cases hit' : i ∈ t' <;>
    simp [Finset.singleton_inter_of_mem, Finset.singleton_inter_of_notMem, hit, hit'] at hi ⊢

omit [Fintype I] in
/-- **The characters trivial on `ε` are the sign characters.** For an orthogonal basis indexed by a
finite type whose generators square to `±1`, every character of the group of signed monomials with
values in a domain of characteristic not two which is trivial on `ε = -1` is the sign character
`χ_t` of exactly one index set `t`. Since every signed monomial squares to `1` or `ε`, such a
character takes the values `±1`, and `t` is the set of indices whose generator goes to `-1`. -/
theorem existsUnique_monomialGroupCharacter_eq [Finite I]
    (hb : (QuadraticMap.associated Q).IsOrthoᵢ b) (hQ : ∀ i, Q (b i) = 1 ∨ Q (b i) = -1)
    {k : Type*} [CommRing k] [IsDomain k] [NeZero (2 : k)] (χ : monomialGroup Q b →* kˣ)
    (hχ : χ (monomialGroupEpsilon Q b) = 1) :
    ∃! t : Finset I,
      (Units.map (Int.castRingHom k : ℤ →* k)).comp (monomialGroupCharacter hb hQ t) = χ := by
  classical
  have := Fintype.ofFinite I
  -- The two integer signs stay distinct in `k`.
  have hcast : Function.Injective (Units.map (Int.castRingHom k : ℤ →* k)) := by
    have h2 : (1 : k) ≠ -1 := fun h ↦ two_ne_zero (α := k) <| by
      rw [← one_add_one_eq_two]
      nth_rewrite 2 [h]
      exact add_neg_cancel 1
    intro u v huv
    have h := congrArg Units.val huv
    rcases Int.units_eq_one_or u with rfl | rfl <;> rcases Int.units_eq_one_or v with rfl | rfl
    · rfl
    · exact (h2 (by simpa using h)).elim
    · exact (h2 (by simpa using h.symm)).elim
    · rfl
  -- Every value of `χ` is a sign, since every signed monomial squares to `1` or `ε`.
  have hsign (x : monomialGroup Q b) : χ x = 1 ∨ χ x = -1 := by
    have hx : (χ x : k) * χ x = 1 := by
      rw [← Units.val_mul, ← map_mul]
      rcases (mem_monomialGroupSign_iff b).mp (mul_self_mem_monomialGroupSign b
          (fun _ _ hij ↦ QuadraticMap.associated_isOrtho.mp (hb hij)) hQ x) with h | h <;>
        simp [h, hχ]
    exact (mul_self_eq_one_iff.mp hx).imp Units.ext Units.ext
  choose g hg using fun i : I ↦ exists_monomialGroup_val_eq_basis hb hQ {i}
  -- The two characters agree on the generators `ε` and `e_i`, hence everywhere.
  have hex : (Units.map (Int.castRingHom k : ℤ →* k)).comp
      (monomialGroupCharacter hb hQ (Finset.univ.filter fun i ↦ χ (g i) = -1)) = χ := by
    refine monomialGroup_hom_ext b (by simp [hχ]) fun x i hx ↦ ?_
    obtain rfl : x = g i := Subtype.ext (Units.ext (by rw [hx, hg, basis_singleton]))
    rw [MonoidHom.comp_apply, monomialGroupCharacter_apply_of_val_eq hb hQ _ (Or.inl (hg i))]
    by_cases hi : χ (g i) = -1
    · simp [Finset.singleton_inter_of_mem, hi]
    · rw [Finset.singleton_inter_of_notMem (by simpa using hi), (hsign (g i)).resolve_right hi]
      simp
  refine ⟨_, hex, fun t ht ↦ monomialGroupCharacter_injective hb hQ
    (MonoidHom.ext fun x ↦ hcast ?_)⟩
  rw [← MonoidHom.comp_apply, ← MonoidHom.comp_apply, ht, hex]

end CliffordAlgebra
